  "verbalization": "Nudifloside B appears to have a mechanism of action that involves targeting the CD276 antigen, which is a receptor expressed on immune cells. This pathway is further mediated by Picrasidine N and Naamidine H, both of which are known to interact with CD276 and ultimately lead to the activation of Thrombopoietin. The evidence suggests a direct, albeit indirect, relationship between Nudifloside B and Thrombopoietin through a series of molecular interactions involving CD276. The scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible pathway, with the final score of 0.5002 suggesting a moderate level of confidence in this mechanistic link. The presence of multiple intermediates, including different compounds that target CD276, supports the idea that Nudifloside B may influence Thrombopoietin through a complex network of interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of CD276 in mediating the effects of Nudifloside B, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the exact role of Thrombopoietin in this context.",
